    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The second equation gives \\(x=16y.\\) Substituting into the first gives \\(8y=y^2,\\) so \\(y(y-8)=0.\\) The condition \\(x\\ne0\\) rules out \\(y=0,\\) leaving \\(y=8\\) and \\(x=128.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(\\frac{x}{4}=4y\\) to express \\(x\\) in terms of \\(y\\)",
        "After substitution, discard the solution that makes \\(x=0\\)"
      ],
